# Source distribution contents. setuptools already adds the package, its
# declared package data, README.md, pyproject.toml and the licence files. By
# default it would also add the top-level tests/test*.py modules without the
# fixtures, conftest and tools they need; the suite runs only from a
# repository checkout (CONTRIBUTING.md), so the sdist ships none of it.
# tools/release/distributions.py fails the release if tests reach the sdist.
prune tests
